<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner in German pulp deal.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner in German pulp deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's Kvaerner ASA said on Wednesday it had entered an agreement with Thyssen Rheinstahl Technik GmbH, Kloeckner Industrie-Anlagen GmbH and Altmark-Industrie AG to form a company to build the world's largest pulp plant.</p>
<p>The plant, to be called Zellstoff Stendal GmbH, will have a capacity of 500,000 tonnes per year of long-fibre pulp and will cost five to six billion crowns.</p>
<p>Kvaerner said the companies' respective investment stakes would be decided at a later date.</p>
<p>Kvaerner's share of the total construction contract would amount to about 2.1 billion crowns, the company said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
